Business Interpretation:
=>Milk production data shows clear seasonal variations and trends over time. 
=>Forecasting future milk production helps dairy industries understand expected increases and decreases in production levels.
=>Accurate forecasting supports better inventory management, storage planning, transportation scheduling, and supply chain optimization. =>Forecast results indicate that production planning can be improved by preparing resources during high-production periods.

Interpretation of Model Comparison:
=>The performance of RNN, LSTM, and GRU models was evaluated using RMSE, MAE, and MAPE metrics.
=>RNN model was able to capture short-term patterns in the data but showed comparatively higher error values. 
=>LSTM model performed better because it can remember long-term dependencies and seasonal patterns using memory cells. GRU model also produced good forecasting results with faster computation due to its simpler architecture.
=>Among all the models, the model with the lowest RMSE and MAE values is considered the best-performing model for milk production forecasting.

Model Justification:
=>The LSTM model was selected as the final forecasting model because it achieved better performance compared to RNN and GRU models. 
=>LSTM is highly suitable for time-series forecasting tasks because it effectively captures long-term trends and seasonal variations present in milk production data.
=>The model generated accurate forecasts and produced lower prediction errors, making it reliable for future milk production forecasting.

Recommendations:
=>Use forecasting models regularly for production planning and decision-making.
=>Increase storage and transportation facilities during peak production months.
=>Optimize inventory management based on forecasted production levels.
=>Implement LSTM-based forecasting systems to reduce wastage and improve operational efficiency.
=>Monitor seasonal production patterns continuously for better business planning.

Conclusion:
Among RNN, LSTM, and GRU models, the model with the lowest RMSE performed best.
LSTM/GRU generally performed better due to their ability to capture long-term dependencies in time series data.